  { number := 183, text := "5. This document MUST NOT replace `0012_Majestic_Memex.md`." },
  { number := 184, text := "" },
  { number := 185, text := "### 4.4 Width template and ones padding" },
  { number := 186, text := "" },
  { number := 187, text := "1. Template bits MUST use the arms in Clause 3.7." },
  { number := 188, text := "2. Template bits MUST pack into whole bytes with bit 7 of each byte consumed first." },
  { number := 189, text := "3. Unused bits in the last template byte MUST be ones." },
  { number := 190, text := "4. A claimed pad that contains a zero MUST be rejected." },
  { number := 191, text := "5. If the last arm's zero is the last bit of a template byte, pad length MUST be zero. That case is perfectly efficient." },
  { number := 192, text := "6. The header MUST store an explicit template bit length (or the byte count of the packed template). Ones padding fills unused bits inside that stored span. Ones padding MUST NOT be treated as a streaming end mark for an uncapped template." },
  { number := 193, text := "7. A walker MUST cap width at 8 payload bytes unless a later published revision names a larger cap. Ones inside the stored span are pad. An unterminated run of ones that would pass that 8 byte cap MUST be rejected, never as pad and never as an infinite arm." },
  { number := 194, text := "" },
  { number := 195, text := "### 4.5 Payload pages" },
  { number := 196, text := "" },
  { number := 197, text := "1. Page 0 MUST have 256 slots." },
  { number := 198, text := "2. Page 1 MUST have 65536 slots." },
  { number := 199, text := "3. A page 1 index MUST be little endian." },
  { number := 200, text := "4. A page 2 or wider index MUST be little endian when present." },
  { number := 201, text := "5. An index greater than or equal to the live size of that page MUST be rejected." },
  { number := 202, text := "6. Huffman codes MUST NOT replace these payload bytes as the lemma spine." },
  { number := 203, text := "7. Huffman coding MAY be measured on a pinned corpus as a length comparison. That measurement MUST NOT change the lemma spine." },
  { number := 204, text := "" },
  { number := 205, text := "### 4.6 Residuals and lossless surface" },
  { number := 206, text := "" },
  { number := 207, text := "1. Encode MUST normalize first, then encode." },
  { number := 208, text := "2. Decode MUST rebuild the original surface, not only the normalized lemmas. The rebuilt surface is the frequency ranked word, shown from the user's spelling table. The rank stays the same. Decode MUST use the user's spelling preference to choose which vocabulary dictionary table supplies the surface spelling, so that spelling can be the regional form. Code and materials on that computer MUST be presented in that preferred spelling at decode time. This selection is a requirement of the encoding. It is not a claim that a converter program is shipped. This item does not specify a spelling table byte layout." },
  { number := 209, text := "3. Runs of space, tab, and other repeated characters MUST be stored in the repeat character residual as (character, count)." },
  { number := 210, text := "4. Capitalization, punctuation, and other marks MUST use the symbol residual, not the repeat character residual." },
  { number := 211, text := "5. Vocabulary tables MUST NOT spend one slot per instance of a repeated indent character." },
  { number := 212, text := "" },
  { number := 213, text := "### 4.7 Encode, decode, and migration" },
  { number := 214, text := "" },
  { number := 215, text := "1. Encode then decode of a well formed input MUST yield the original surface for the pinned rule set." },
  { number := 216, text := "2. A later table set MUST NOT be accepted unless a Lean check shows that re-encoding every document in the pinned corpus is not longer than the previous encoding." },
  { number := 217, text := "3. The pinned corpus and the exact Lean predicate remain Residual until the operator names them." },
  { number := 218, text := "4. Systems Lean is the language in which that predicate SHALL later be stated. This document does not claim Slake typechecks the package." },
  { number := 219, text := "" },
  { number := 220, text := "### 4.8 Stack program" },
  { number := 221, text := "" },
  { number := 222, text := "1. A stack program MUST be able to hold a bit cursor and a byte cursor." },
  { number := 223, text := "2. This document MUST NOT publish an instruction listing for that program." },
