  { number := 252, text := "6. Page 0 has 256 slots; page 1 has 65536 slots; multi byte indices are little endian; payload is bytes; Huffman coding is not the lemma spine (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 253, text := "7. Encode normalizes first then encodes; decode rebuilds the original surface; decode uses the user's spelling preference to choose the vocabulary dictionary table so the surface spelling can be the regional form; code and materials on that computer are presented in that preferred spelling at decode time; that selection is not a claim that a converter program is shipped; repeat character residual is a plane of (character, count); symbol residual is separate (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 254, text := "8. Encode then decode yields the original surface; a later table is accepted only when a Lean check shows the new encoding is not longer on a pinned corpus (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 255, text := "9. No instruction listing for the stack program is published (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 256, text := "10. Every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean`; proofs of those encodings live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`; the named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 257, text := "11. ENKI is the index and is not this bitstream; ENKI has no numbered specification (Clause 1 and Clause 3.2)." },
  { number := 258, text := "12. A conforming encoder is not claimed. A spelling converter program is not claimed." },
  { number := 259, text := "" },
  { number := 260, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming encoder. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped codec." },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) and the MAY Huffman measurement do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to." },
  { number := 263, text := "" },
  { number := 264, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 265, text := "" },
  { number := 266, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. Checkable residual claims live in `lean/ResidualClaims.lean`, and this specification still carries its own residual clause." },
  { number := 267, text := "" },
  { number := 268, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 269, text := "" },
  { number := 270, text := "1. RDPS is unpublished. This document does not assign RDPS a number and does not create a numbered file for it." },
  { number := 271, text := "2. FilterScript is unpublished. This document does not assign FilterScript a number and does not create a numbered file for it." },
  { number := 272, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 273, text := "4. Number 0015 is not assigned in this document. This document MUST NOT steal number 0015. The next unassigned number after this specification is 0015. Number 0015 is not Anunnaki Encoding." },
  { number := 274, text := "5. ENKI has no numbered specification. This document MUST NOT be read as creating `NNNN_ENKI.md`." },
  { number := 275, text := "6. fargo has no numbered specification and no assigned number." },
  { number := 276, text := "7. Lake wiring for this specification is in this repository: encodings in `lean/AnunnakiSpec.lean`, proofs in `lean/AnunnakiProofs.lean`, sibling `0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.lean`, and the `anunnaki_tests` check. Catalog tokens Anunnaki, bitstream, and ENKI live in `0005_CATE.md` and `aspell_words.txt`. This specification does not claim a conforming encoder." },
  { number := 277, text := "" },
  { number := 278, text := "### 6.2 Product that is not implemented" },
  { number := 279, text := "" },
  { number := 280, text := "1. Anunnaki Encoding work is ongoing. A conforming encoder is not claimed. This specification records the contract. It does not ship an encoder. It does not ship a spelling converter program." },
  { number := 281, text := "2. This specification does not define a stack program instruction set. Emission of such a program from Lean Machine is not claimed." },
  { number := 282, text := "3. Nested language (English containing Lean containing a string) is in scope and is not specified here." },
  { number := 283, text := "4. The on disk join from CATE WordID to Anunnaki rank is not specified here. Existence of that join is locked. On disk shape is not. The byte layout of a spelling table is not specified here. The isomorphism between those tables and the preference that selects a table at decode are specified in Clause 3.5, Clause 3.11, Clause 4.1, Clause 4.2, and Clause 4.6." },
  { number := 284, text := "5. The pinned corpus for Clause 4.7 is not named here. The corpus remains Residual." },
  { number := 285, text := "6. Compound word and technical term rules per language are not specified here." },
  { number := 286, text := "7. Whether Anunnaki is default `.majestic` text or a later `memex compress` command is not specified here." },
  { number := 287, text := "8. Who emits the stack program is not specified here." },
  { number := 288, text := "" },
  { number := 289, text := "### 6.3 Fixtures and languages that remain unpinned" },
  { number := 290, text := "" },
  { number := 291, text := "1. v2 fixtures cover English and Lean 4 only." },
  { number := 292, text := "2. C is named and unpinned." },
  { number := 293, text := "3. Rust 1 is an unpinned grammar name." },
  { number := 294, text := "4. Nix is named and unpinned." },
  { number := 295, text := "5. C++ is named and unpinned." },
  { number := 296, text := "6. Huffman versus pages length on a real corpus is not measured here." },
  { number := 297, text := "" },
  { number := 298, text := "### 6.4 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 299, text := "" },
  { number := 300, text := "1. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration remain ongoing and not ready for use. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 301, text := "2. `lean/AnunnakiSpec.lean` encodes selected claims. `lean/AnunnakiProofs.lean` proves those claims. `0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0014.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that a conforming encoder exists. They are not a proof that a spelling converter program is shipped. They are not a proof that CATE, SSSSS, or Majestic Memex are replaced." },
  { number := 302, text := "3. Leftover residual facts in Clause 6.1 and Clause 6.2 are encoded in `lean/AnunnakiSpec.lean`. Proofs that leftover clashes are Cons False live in `lean/AnunnakiProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 303, text := "" },
  { number := 304, text := "### 6.5 Leftover clashes that are Cons False" },
  { number := 305, text := "" },
  { number := 306, text := "1. Treating ENKI and Anunnaki Encoding as one object is Cons False in `lean/AnunnakiProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 307, text := "2. Claiming a conforming encoder is Cons False in that same module. Claiming a spelling converter program is Cons False in that same module." },
  { number := 308, text := "3. Treating number 0015 as this specification is Cons False in that same module. This document MUST NOT create `0015_*.md`." },
  { number := 309, text := "4. Treating the Carbonado Network Protocol as assigned a number here is Cons False in that same module. Carbonado stays unnumbered." },
  { number := 310, text := "5. Treating ENKI as having a numbered specification is Cons False in that same module. This document MUST NOT create `NNNN_ENKI.md`." },
  { number := 311, text := "6. Treating RDPS as assigned a number here is Cons False in that same module." },
  { number := 312, text := "7. Treating FilterScript as assigned a number here is Cons False in that same module. Treating a dialect as needing its own LanguageID is Cons False in that same module." },
  { number := 313, text := "" },
  { number := 314, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 315, text := "" },
  { number := 316, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260920" },
  { number := 317, text := "" },
  { number := 318, text := "First publication of Anunnaki Encoding as numbered specification 0014 with file name `0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.md`. Records ENKI as the index and Anunnaki as the bitstream. Records that this specification does not replace CATE (`0005_CATE.md`), SSSSS (`0004_SSSSS.md`), or Majestic Memex (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`). Records width arms `0` / `10` / `110` / `1110`, ones padding that rejects a claimed pad containing a zero, bit 7 first, payload cap of 8 bytes, page 0 of 256 slots, page 1 of 65536 slots with little endian indices, repeat character residual as a plane of (character, count), separate symbol residual, normalize first then encode, decode that rebuilds the original surface, Huffman coding as measurement and not the lemma spine, and migration accepted only when a Lean check shows the new encoding is not longer. Records that a conforming encoder is not claimed. Records unpublished RDPS, FilterScript, and Carbonado Network Protocol. Records that number 0015 is not this specification. Records leftover clashes as Cons False in `lean/AnunnakiProofs.lean` for treating ENKI and Anunnaki Encoding as one object, claiming a conforming encoder, treating number 0015 as this specification, treating Carbonado as numbered, and treating ENKI, RDPS, or FilterScript as assigned a number here. Records that one language keeps one LanguageID, that a dialect does not get a different LanguageID, that variations of spelling are an isomorphism between vocabulary dictionary tables, and that the frequency ranked word number stays the same across those tables. Records that decode uses the user's spelling preference to choose the table, so code and materials on that computer are presented in that preferred spelling. Records that this selection is a requirement of the encoding and is not a claim that a converter program is shipped. Records that the byte layout of a spelling table is not specified. Records that treating a dialect as needing its own LanguageID is Cons False in that same module. Records that ones inside the stored span are pad and that an unterminated run of ones that would pass the 8 byte cap is rejected. Records that the rebuilt surface is the frequency ranked word, shown from the user's spelling table, and that the rank stays the same. Records that claiming a spelling converter program is Cons False in that same module." },
  { number := 319, text := "" },
